UID:10000871-1795082400-1795107600@hatefreetogether.org
SUMMARY:Manetti Shrem Museum: Together Again\, 1960–2026\, Perspectives from UC Davis’ Fine Arts Collection
DESCRIPTION:Together Again inaugurates the Manetti Shrem Museum’s ongoing collection galleries. This exhibition highlighting the collection will be on long-term view\, accompanied by temporary exhibitions each fall and winter. \nThe ongoing collection galleries trace a history of art forged from UC Davis and throughout Northern California. By focusing on relationships of many kinds\, this presentation proposes that in order to understand an artwork in all its fullness\, chance encounters and long-standing friendships often matter as much as formal affiliations. UC Davis legends such as Wayne Thiebaud\, Deborah Butterfield and Bruce Nauman are exhibited alongside important regional voices that were once overlooked\, and the exhibition extends to the artists shaping Northern California today\, including Sadie Barnette\, Woody De Othello and Ruby Neri. Together Again builds bridges between who we were and who we are becoming at UC Davis\, and affirms the Manetti Shrem Museum as home to the complex story of Northern California art — rich in legacy and always in the process of becoming. \nThe collection will be open Wednesdays to Sundays\, 10 a.m. to 5 p.m. The location is the Jan Shrem and Maria Manetti Shrem Museum of Art at UC Davis. Admission is free.
URL:https://hatefreetogether.org/event/together-again-1960-2026-perspectives-from-uc-davis-fine-arts-collection/2026-11-19/
LOCATION:Jan Shrem and Maria Manetti Shrem Museum of Art at UC Davis\, 254 Old Davis Road\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Season of Connection
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://hatefreetogether.org/wp-content/uploads/ta-title-social.webp
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visityolo Event": "https://visityolo.com/event/portraits-of-things-paintings-by-gioia-fonda-and-charlie-gill/2026-11-19/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visityolo_event
X-SOURCE:Visityolo Event
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T170000
DTSTAMP:20260928T180906Z
CREATED:20260928T180906Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T180906Z
UID:10014947-1795087800-1795107600@visityolo.com
SUMMARY:Portraits of Things: Paintings by Gioia Fonda and Charlie Gill
DESCRIPTION:Portraits of Things: Paintings by Gioia Fonda and Charlie Gill at Pence Gallery in Davis \nExhibit: October 9 – November 29\, 2026 \nReception: Friday\, October 9\, 6-9 PM (Free) \nArtist Talk: Sunday\, November 8\, 2-3:30 PM (Free) \n  \nInterdisciplinary artist Gioia Fonda has long collected colorful toys\, both for their intrinsic charm and as creative inspiration. As a student at California College of the Arts\, she arranged small collectibles into still-life compositions\, captured them on film\, and processed the photos at a local drugstore. Captivated by these arrangements\, her advisor\, Charlie Gill\, painted spare compositions based on her photographs—works that now hang alongside hers. For this exhibition\, Fonda has created a series of new paintings featuring similar arrangements of toys and found objects. She is also offering an opportunity for members of the public to exhibit their own small works on paper\, riffing on some of her recent photos. Artists may add to this display throughout the duration of the show.  \n  \nSponsored by the Pence Community Curatorial Fund. \n  \nImage: Gioia Fonda\, “Holding It Together”
URL:https://visityolo.com/event/portraits-of-things-paintings-by-gioia-fonda-and-charlie-gill/2026-11-19/
LOCATION:Pence Gallery\, 212 D Street\, Davis\, CA 95616
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visityolo.com/wp-content/uploads/Gioia-Fonda-Holding-It-Together-copy.jpeg
ORGANIZER;CN="Pence Gallery":MAILTO:pencesocialmedia@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
